{
  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200 + multiprofile is the clear best pipeline (acc ~0.65), while image-only with resnet50 is very weak (acc 0.208). The critical open question is whether adding image features to the best RNA pipeline provides any benefit, or whether image is simply uninformative for this task. This experiment (config_030: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) takes the best RNA configuration and adds the simplest possible image contribution (concat fusion with resnet50). It tests one focused question: does image add signal on top of scvi_n200 multiprofile RNA? If performance drops or stays flat, we can eliminate the large multimodal search space and focus budget on refining the RNA pipeline. If it improves, we confirm a multimodal direction and know where to invest next. This is the highest-information-per-experiment choice because it gates ~30+ downstream configurations, and it changes only the minimal set of variables (adding image + concat) relative to the proven best RNA-only setup."
}

